  14:     shape: each motif fits in a 3x3 bbox (area 4-8 cells), color monochrome, connected (8-conn) [observed]
  15:     colors: matching motifs share color with a dst block; distractors use other non-bg colors (each motif color unique in input)
  16:     layout: rectangular grid (2x3, 3x2, 4x2 observed) of 3x3 slots spaced by 4 cells (3 body + 1 gap)
  17:     slot_fill: slots filled >= count(matching+distractors); 0-2 empty slots allowed [observed]
  18:     region: separated from dst region (non-overlap on at least one of {row-range, col-range})
  19:   output:
  20:     shape: (1 + R*5 + (R-1) + 1) x (1 + C*5 + (C-1) + 1) based on dst grid RxC
  21:     content: each 5x5 block carved by stamping its matching motif (centered at offset (1,1) within 5x5) as bg holes; motif cells -> bg, rest keep block color; blocks packed with 1-cell gaps preserving input row/col order; 1-cell bg border
